{"adjusted_val_bpb": -2.6336330579639795, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No integrity problems. The diff doesn't read files, paste coordinates or use the test inputs. All randomness comes from the seeded rng. The exact validity check is still guarded by the unchanged _repair step and the np.clip of the centres.", "No bug that would make the result meaningless. On odd iterations the melt branch starts from the incumbent: it jitters the centres (clipped to [0.02, 0.98]), caps the radii at melt in [0.07, 0.11], and runs the cap schedule from melt up to 1.0. The cap list is never empty because it always ends with 1.0. Half of the restarts still start from random points.", "Recomputed z: with noise sd 0.0023 and one run on each side, the standard error is 0.0023*sqrt(2) \u2248 0.00325. The difference is 0.0007 in the candidate's disfavour, so z \u2248 -0.215. The harness gives -0.192. The gap is consistent with the displayed values being rounded to 4 decimals, and the sign and conclusion are the same.", "The evidence is weak: n=1 for both candidate and incumbent. The candidate (2.6336) is within noise of the incumbent (2.6343), so 'reject' is reasonable, but it does not show that melt-and-regrow is harmful. A replicate could be justified if slots allow."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Adds a melt-and-regrow restart on every other loop iteration: the best packing's centres get sd-0.01 jitter, radii are capped at a seeded MELT_CAP in [0.07, 0.11], and the cap continuation runs only from MELT_CAP upward, with the other iterations left as plain random restarts.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "willow", "idea_id": "b015", "incumbent_after": {"mean": -2.634251375190989, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": -2.634251375190989, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B2_p26_HH_2_s0-candidate-6_1795057689923", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.002